==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*eri}}, derived from {{m|fiu-fin-pro|*erä}} (see {{m|fi|erä}} for more). Cognate with {{cog|et|eri}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation}}

===Adjective===
{{fi-adj}} {{tlb|fi|not comparable|indeclinable}}

# [[different]], [[other]], [[another]]
#: {{ux|fi|Se on '''eri''' sana.|That's a '''different''' / an'''other''' word.}}
# [[different]], [[separate]]

====Inflection====
The cases of ''eri'' are used only as adverbs.
{{fi-decl-pron|pos=adj|1s=[[eri-]]|8p=[[erillään]]|10p=[[erilleen]]|12p=[[erikseen]]|a8p=[[erittäin]]}}

In colloquial language, ''eri'' may sometimes be inflected as a regular adjective. This is considered nonstandard.
{{fi-decl-risti|pos=adj|er|||ä}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|separate}} {{l|fi|erillinen}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|fi|olla}} ''eri'' {{l|fi|mieli|mieltä}} {{l|fi|joku|jonkun}} {{l|fi|kanssa}} = to [[disagree]] with sb
* ''eri'' {{l|fi|tapa|tavalla}} = in a [[different]] [[manner]], in a different [[way]]
* ''eri'' {{l|fi|tapa|tavoin}} = in [[different]]/[[many]] [[manner]]s, in different/many [[way]]s
* adjectives: {{l|fi|erikoinen}}, {{l|fi|erilainen}}, {{l|fi|erillinen}}, {{l|fi|erinäinen}}, {{l|fi|erityinen}}, {{l|fi|eriävä}}
* verbs: {{l|fi|eristää}}, {{l|fi|eritä}}, {{l|fi|eriyttää}}

===Adverb===
{{head|fi|adverb}}

# {{lb|fi|rare}} [[really]], [[truly]]
#: {{ux|fi|Olet '''eri''' hyvä kaveri.|You're a ''really'' good friend.}}

